{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqaaf1ox5pn","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Bounded traversal experiment design: trigger only on why / what-caused intent queries with no task key; RAG top hit becomes anchor; expand ancestor blocker decision edges max 2 hops; deterministic edge-type scoring; compare against flat RAG on heldout bench before any further investment.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T02:08:30.805Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqaaf1ox5pn","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Anchored vs anchorless retrieval are different problems: DAG first when task known, RAG as anchor finder when not","summary":"DECISION (user-approved 2026-06-11, from review of external agent memory search proposal). Two retrieval pipelines are inversions of one principle: structure outranks similarity once you have a foothold. (1) ANCHORED retrieval (agent on a known task): keep our existing DAG-first design — context deps inject ungated at score 1.0, RAG fills remaining slots. The external proposal's RAG-first spark search would be strictly worse here: it re-derives via cosine what an edge already states. (2) ANCHORLESS retrieval (free-text \"why did X fail?\" with no task key): our system currently degrades to pure flat RAG — this is the gap. Fix: use RAG only to FIND the anchor node, then hand off to bounded DAG edge traversal (max 2 hops, ancestor / blocker / decision edges, deterministic scoring, NO LLM and NO learned model in the loop). Rejected for now: iterative multi-spark backtracking, learned spark/path/stop scorers — KB too sparse (coverage-bottlenecked, kb_earned 13%) and traces too few; iterative LLM-scored search also attacks the abstain-by-default cost-parity result. NEXT: run heldout bench test of bounded traversal vs flat RAG on why/causal queries — if no score lift, drop the traversal idea cheaply.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T02:08:30.801Z","vec":[-0.09400393813848495,0.02999366819858551,0.01981184631586075,0.033048443496227264,0.004878803621977568,-0.057800885289907455,0.02580280415713787,-0.02396334521472454,0.0008867246215231717,-0.011048013344407082,0.0011666727950796485,0.08130177110433578,0.026365268975496292,-0.027827410027384758,-0.03534349426627159,0.059199605137109756,0.06837546080350876,0.04599130526185036,-0.033047664910554886,-0.026646409183740616,-0.026118062436580658,-0.024128440767526627,0.019669484347105026,-0.0411523